    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/clinical-assistant-associate-professor-gf9902-tulsa-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GF9902",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GF9902 - Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GF9902 - Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GF9902 Apply Now Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor GF9902 494443 Tulsa CENTER FOR HEALTH SCIENCES (CHS) Faculty Master's degree Campus OSU-Center for Health Sciences Contact Name & Email Jamie Childers, Jamie.Childers@okstate.edu Work Schedule Typically, Monday - Friday 8 hour shifts Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range $ salary Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by to ensure full consideration. About this Position Job Description: Principal Faculty supports the Program Director in ensuring all aspects of the Program meet the Standards of Accreditation set forth by the ARC-PA. Principal faculty also ensures curriculum is consistent with current practice standards as it relates to the PA role in providing patient care and Oklahoma State University policies. This position is a Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor, non-tenure track. Responsibilities Administrative responsibilities, Required Assists in aligning programmatic operations with accreditation standards Participates in program evaluation and assessment activities Assists in reviewing and revising the program’s mission, goals, and competencies Academic Responsibilities, Required Evaluates student progress and performance at regular intervals Assures the availability of remedial instruction Provides academic counseling and advising students Provides classroom and laboratory instruction Service, Required Participate in student recruitment and the admission review and selection process Advocates for the Program within the University, community clinical partners, as well as state and national organizations Serves on committees, both internal and external to the institution, as approved by the program director Clinical Practice, recommended but not required Provide medical care within an OSU sponsored clinic Dedicated to serving as a PA student preceptor Reporting structure This position uses a dual reporting structure: To the PA Program Director for accreditation, curriculum, programmatic assessment, and operations. To the Department Chair for institutional faculty responsibilities, evaluation, and HR processes. Required Qualifications Master's (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Clinical experience of two or more years working full-time as a physician assistant Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: NCCPA certification Current State License preferably with current DEA, OBNDD license Preferred Qualifications Teaching experience, with an emphasis in PA education Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: ACLS, BLS, PALS certification Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Knowledge and understanding of PA program organization and administration Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills Leadership skills demonstrated by participation in local, regional or national PA programs Clinical Practice, recommended but not required Provide medical care within an OSU sponsored clinic Dedicated to serving as a PA student preceptor All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 7563295e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Faculty/Instructor Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Center for Health Sciences OSU-Center for Health Sciences Minimum Education Level Master's degree Master's degree First Name (required) 4addd9a7 Last Name (required) 0bc16d7e Email (required) 8a16ccc7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) d6649152 Last Name (required) 6290dcff Email (required) 53cf3ecc Save this job for later ef733cd9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubs