    "https://jobs.okstate.edu/jobs/clinical-psychology-postdoctoral-psychology-fellow-gf1738-tulsa-oklahoma-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Psychology Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow- GF1738",
      "description": "Clinical Psychology Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow- GF1738 - Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Clinical Psychology Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow- GF1738 - Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Psychology Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow- GF1738 Apply Now Clinical Psychology Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow- GF1738 495243 Tulsa CENTER FOR HEALTH SCIENCES (CHS) Adjunct/Temp Faculty PhD Campus OSU-Center for Health Sciences Contact Name & Email Jeffery Kellerman, jeff.kellerman@okstate.edu Work Schedule Monday through Friday, 8:00am-5:00pm with occasional evenings and weekends. Appointment Length Regular Continuous/Until Further Notice Hiring Range Commensurate with experience and credentials Priority Application Date While applications will be accepted until a successful candidate has been hired, interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials by to ensure full consideration. Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, please include a resume, cover letter and contact information for three professional references. About this Position The Clinical Psychology Postdoctoral Psychology Fellow position will be housed within the OSU Behavioral Medicine Clinic, part of the Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Sciences. This is a 12-month, full-time training program designed to meet the Oklahoma State Board of Examiners of Psychologists’ postdoctoral supervision and training requirements for licensure. The fellowship provides comprehensive clinical experience under the direct supervision of licensed psychologists, with opportunities to refine assessment, therapy, and consultation skills across diverse client populations. The postdoctoral fellow will have the opportunity to provide psychological assessment and evidence-based therapy services to children, adolescents, and/or adults in an outpatient medical setting. Training experiences will be individualized to align with the fellow’s professional interests and career goals, with opportunities to specialize in areas such as integrated behavioral health, trauma, neuropsychological assessment, and school-based services. Additional professional development activities will include didactic seminars, supervision of trainees, multidisciplinary collaboration, and participation in program development. This position offers rich exposure to interdisciplinary practice within a medical setting and is ideal for individuals seeking a broad-based clinical and professional experience leading to independent licensure. Required Qualifications Ph.D./Ed.D. Ph.D. or Psy.D. in Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology from an APA- or CPA-accredited program. Degree must be conferred prior to the fellowship start date (degree must be conferred on or before agreed upon start date) Demonstrated competence in psychological assessment and intervention with children and/or adults Certifications, Registrations, and/or Licenses: Completion of an APA- or CPA-accredited predoctoral internship Eligibility for postdoctoral supervision toward licensure in the State of Oklahoma Preferred Qualifications Experience working in medical, academic, or interdisciplinary behavioral health settings Interest in neuropsychological assessment or school psychology Skills, Proficiencies, and/or Knowledge: Strong commitment to evidence-based practice, diversity, and interdisciplinary collaboration Working Conditions Office environment. Physical Requirements Ability to lift and carry 20 pounds, stoop, reach, stand, walk, finger, grasp, feel, talk, hear, see, and perform repetitive motions with or without reasonable accommodations. All positions are subject to the availability of funding, and any offers are contingent upon the successful completion of a background check. Federal law requires employers to provide reasonable accommodation to qualified individuals with disabilities. Please tell us if you require a reasonable accommodation in the application process. Examples of reasonable accommodation include making a change to the application process, providing documents in an alternate format, using a sign language interpreter, or using specialized equipment. To request an accommodation, please email eeo@okstate.edu or call 405-744-5449. Oklahoma State University, as an equal opportunity employer, complies with all applicable federal and state laws regarding non-discrimination. Oklahoma State University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity for all individuals and does not discriminate based on race, religion, age, sex, color, national origin, marital status, disability, or veteran status with regard to employment, educational programs and activities, and/or admissions. For more information, visit eeo.okstate.edu. Sign Up for job alerts Job Alert 74d82a94 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty/Instructor Medical & Health-Related Faculty/Instructor Medical & Health-Related Employment Type Adjunct/Temp Faculty Adjunct/Temp Faculty Locations Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Tulsa, Oklahoma, United States Posting Campus OSU-Center for Health Sciences OSU-Center for Health Sciences Minimum Education Level PhD PhD First Name (required) c01eee64 Last Name (required) 21b4516d Email (required) cd978a39 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about employment within the OSU/A&M System. Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies. Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to all system campus privacy policies. Thank you Save this job for later First Name (required) d9ab59a9 Last Name (required) d0895c0d Em